md, the Markdown reader
=======================

What md renders, one example of each (see man md). Lines of prose that follow 
each other are one paragraph, wrapped at 78 columns.


Lists and quotes
----------------

  - a bullet item, whose continuation line joins the item
  - a second item with code and a link (/MAN/MD)

  1. a numbered item
  2. and another

  | a quoted line


Code and tables
---------------

--More--          dir -R /BIN     a code block: verbatim, indented


  command        what it shows     
  -------------  ----------------  
  md FILE.MD     the file, styled  
  md -p FILE.MD  the same, plain   

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The end.
/> 
/> 
usage: md [-p] FILE.MD    render markdown (-p: no ANSI styling); md with no file lists /DOCS
  MDDEMO.MD
  OS.MD
  Y1CC.MD
